  {
   "query": "queries.scm",
   "capabilities": [
    "references",
    "definitions"
   ],
   "reason": "This grammar holds every JavaScript expression as one opaque `javascript` token, so an interpolation `#{user.name}`, an unquoted attribute value `href=url`, a loop's iterator and a condition are not stated as references to anything, and a name bound by `- var x = 1` is not declared."
  },
  {
   "query": "queries.scm",
   "capabilities": [
    "references"
   ],
   "reason": "An `extends` or `include` path is kept exactly as written. Pug resolves it against the renderer's `basedir` and appends `.pug` when the extension is omitted, so the path here is not a file this Pack can point at."
  },
  {
   "query": "queries.scm",
   "capabilities": [
    "definitions",
    "references"
   ],
   "reason": "A block overridden by `block`, `append` or `prepend` is recorded by name only; which layout in the `extends` chain declared it is not resolved, and a mixin called before it is defined is not distinguished from one defined in an included file."
  },
  {
   "query": "queries.scm",
   "capabilities": [
    "references"
   ],
   "reason": "A filter such as `:markdown-it` names a jstransformer package, not anything declared in Pug, and the text it transforms is passed through untouched rather than parsed as the language the filter implies."
  }
